1
00:00:00,017 --> 00:00:02,164
So I asked the obvious question:

2
00:00:02,204 --> 00:00:04,685
why not digital money without a bank? A file.

3
00:00:04,725 --> 00:00:05,711
You send it, done.

4
00:00:05,751 --> 00:00:08,041
The problem is that anything digital can be copied.

5
00:00:08,081 --> 00:00:11,310
A photo, a song, a movie. Copy, paste. Free.

6
00:00:11,350 --> 00:00:12,310
If money were a file,

7
00:00:12,350 --> 00:00:14,773
Alice could send the same hundred dollars to Bob,

8
00:00:14,813 --> 00:00:16,230
and to Carol. At once.

9
00:00:16,270 --> 00:00:17,886
That is called the double-spending problem.

10
00:00:17,926 --> 00:00:19,172
And that is why they needed someone in the

11
00:00:19,212 --> 00:00:21,463
middle, keeping track of who paid what.

12
00:00:21,503 --> 00:00:23,017
Humans had been trying since the eighties.

13
00:00:23,057 --> 00:00:25,793
A scientist named David Chaum started a digital cash company.

14
00:00:25,833 --> 00:00:27,494
It went bankrupt in 1998.

15
00:00:27,534 --> 00:00:29,375
The digital money ran out of money.

16
00:00:29,415 --> 00:00:32,986
This problem went unsolved for years until an anonymous

17
00:00:33,026 --> 00:00:34,380
stranger solved it.

18
00:00:34,420 --> 00:00:36,636
The whole story is on the Earth Report channel.

19
00:00:36,708 --> 00:00:38,348
Subscribe to the channel and turn on the bell

20
00:00:38,388 --> 00:00:41,177
so my secret reports on your planet reach you first.
